    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "anchor": "drill",
      "item": "techguns:ore_drill_head_medium_steel",
      "text": "An ore drill item is required for the drill to work. Depending on the size of the multiblock a different drill size is required. In the gui when hovering the progress bar the radius of the drill is shown. A Radius of 0 (just controller and rod) needs a small drill, radius 1 and 2 require a medium drill, while 3 and 4 need a large drill.",
      "title": "Drill Item"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "anchor": "drill",
      "item": "techguns:ore_drill_head_medium_obsidian_steel",
      "text": "The material of the drill defines the mining level of the drill. Iron has a mininglevel of 1, obsidian steel 2 and carbon 3.",
      "title": "Drill Item"
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "The drill multiblock can be powered by cables or by inputting items that can be used as furnace fuel or liquid fuel. The power from items is calculated from the furnace burn time. Liquid fuel burn value is defined in the config file. Every fluid that is defined as 'fuel' in the config file is added with the same burn value. Formulas are explained $(l:ore_drills/ore_clusters#power)here$(/l).",
      "title": "Power"
    }
  ]
